ll producing one card. That can be replicated either way:\n- If we seed 3 once and never re-seed: 52000 deals of one card from a fresh deck = 52000 lrand48 calls\n- If `create_shuffled_deck` re-seeds: each call to create deck would also call srand48 = nope that wouldn't match\n\nThe first option matches. So:\n- Either `create_shuffled_deck` starts at seed 3 the first time only, OR\n- The seed is implicitly set to 3 globally somewhere\n\nBut the test is called `test_card_operations` and runs ALL the prior phases first which consume RNG state. Yet expected_card_count = 1001, 1012, 1032, ... which matches starting from seed 3 fresh.\n\nWait, maybe `create_shuffled_deck` always re-seeds? Let me check:"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":303,"cache_read_input_tokens":64054,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":303,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2196daa1-2ca2-4db2-aef8-d08cd17e88c3","uuid":"ca30a93b-41ef-4c8c-935d-c58a89dee727"}
